<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Acetabularia acetabulum Turing wavelength at 25.28 µm (Holocene, detail scale) (Acetabularia acetabulum)",
        "Acetabularia acetabulum Turing wavelength at 25.28 µm (Holocene, detail scale) faithfully reproduces Acetabularia acetabulum morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Acetabularia acetabulum specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Acetabularia acetabulum" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A successor chronospecies. The Acetabularia series in this slot is Holocene only.",
        "does_not_claim: That sibling slot 192 parameters were reused.",
        "does_not_claim: That the gallery plate or the CC0 photograph is a calibrated micrograph of 25.28 µm pigment stripes.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Face-on tiling of the periodic patch into an 88-ridge young cap of radius 354 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Inhibitor axial/hoop diffusivity ratio 0.45, which selects axial ridges.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Nominal A, B and diffusivities that place the fastest mode on the 25.28 µm tier length.",
        "reported_in_source: Dumais & Harrison 2000: Acetabularia whorls are the pattern for which reaction-diffusion is the mechanism the experiments favour.",
        "reported_in_source: Holloway & Harrison 2007: a Brusselator on a growing plant surface produces whorled branches.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: 25.28 µm is the MorphoEval tier length, not a spacing measured by Dumais & Harrison.",
        "transfer_boundary: The CC0 photograph is an adult cap; the model cap is the 0.71 mm disk implied by 88 ridges at 25.28 µm." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Acetabularia acetabulum" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Acetabularia" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/acetabularia_acetabulum_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Acetabularia acetabulum; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.x, note Cloud agent VM; no project venv. Cryptographic nanopub signing unavailable (~/.nanopub/profile.yml absent).; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber. | Dumais & Harrison 2000: Acetabularia whorls are the pattern for which reaction-diffusion is the mechanism the experiments favour. | Holloway & Harrison 2007: a Brusselator on a growing plant surface produces whorled branches.; reconstructed_in_script: Nominal A, B and diffusivities that place the fastest mode on the 25.28 µm tier length. | Inhibitor axial/hoop diffusivity ratio 0.45, which selects axial ridges. | Face-on tiling of the periodic patch into an 88-ridge young cap of radius 354 µm.; transfer_boundary: 25.28 µm is the MorphoEval tier length, not a spacing measured by Dumais & Harrison. | The CC0 photograph is an adult cap; the model cap is the 0.71 mm disk implied by 88 ridges at 25.28 µm.; does_not_claim: That the gallery plate or the CC0 photograph is a calibrated micrograph of 25.28 µm pigment stripes. | A successor chronospecies. The Acetabularia series in this slot is Holocene only. | That sibling slot 192 parameters were reused.]; phenomenon_size: 41 µm (4.096e-05 m, log10=-4.388 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 41 µm to 6.7 cm): 41 µm:acetabularia-acetabulum-bioelectric-polarity, 79 µm:acetabularia-acetabulum-vertex-packing, 1.5 mm:acetabularia-acetabulum-turing-wavelength, 2.8 mm:acetabularia-acetabulum-clock-wavefront, 6.3 mm:acetabularia-acetabulum-elastic-buckling, 8.7 mm:acetabularia-acetabulum-morphogen-condensation, 1.1 cm:acetabularia-acetabulum-flux-canalization, 1.5 cm:acetabularia-acetabulum-branching-tree" ;
